/// Static, human-readable API documentation for the route-recorder backend.
/// Exposed as a single `getApiDoc` query so the service is discoverable.
mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Route Recorder Backend API\n\nBackend for a Waze-style GPS route recorder and live navigator. It stores each user's recorded routes, their street tags/notes, and their preferred travel mode. All data is scoped per user: a caller can only read and mutate records it owns.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\nEvery public method below requires a signed (non-anonymous) caller. The frontend authenticates with Internet Identity and pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent that already holds the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nThere is no separate registration step: the first time a caller invokes any method, it is treated as its own owner scope. An anonymous caller receives a trap on every method, for example `Unauthorized: sign in to view your routes`. A signed-in principal derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered, so it sees its own (empty) data rather than the other principal's records.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- `RouteId` and `TagId` are `Nat` identifiers assigned by the backend.\n- `distanceMeters` is a `Float` in meters.\n- `durationSeconds` is a `Nat` in seconds.\n- `startedAt`, `endedAt`, and `createdAt` are `Nat` Unix timestamps in nanoseconds (from `Time.now()`).\n- `lat` and `lng` are `Float` decimal degrees (WGS84).\n- `mode` is a variant: `#car`, `#bus`, `#motorcycle`, `#bicycle`, `#walking`.\n- `category` is a variant: `#pothole`, `#hazard`, `#speedCamera`, `#trafficSignal`, `#note`.\n- `points` is an array of `{ lat : Float; lng : Float; timestamp : Nat }` path samples.\n\n## Routes\n\n- `listRoutes() : async [Route]` — query; returns the caller's saved routes.\n- `getRoute(id : RouteId) : async ?Route` — query; returns one route or `null`.\n- `addRoute(input : RouteInput) : async RouteId` — update; saves a newly recorded route and returns its new id.\n- `updateRoute(id : RouteId, update : RouteUpdate) : async ?Route` — update; renames a route and/or changes its travel mode. Returns the updated route, or `null` if the caller does not own that id.\n- `deleteRoute(id : RouteId) : async Bool` — update; deletes the route and returns `true` when a route was removed, `false` otherwise.\n\n## Tags and notes\n\n- `listTags() : async [Tag]` — query; returns the caller's tags and notes.\n- `getTag(id : TagId) : async ?Tag` — query; returns one tag or `null`.\n- `addTag(input : TagInput) : async TagId` — update; creates a tag/note at an exact map point and returns its new id. `createdAt` is set server-side.\n- `updateTag(id : TagId, update : TagUpdate) : async ?Tag` — update; edits a tag's category and/or note. Returns the updated tag, or `null` if not owned.\n- `deleteTag(id : TagId) : async Bool` — update; deletes the tag and returns `true` when a tag was removed, `false` otherwise.\n\n## Travel mode preference\n\n- `getTravelMode() : async TravelMode` — query; returns the caller's persisted travel mode, defaulting to `#car` when never set.\n- `setTravelMode(mode : TravelMode) : async TravelMode` — update; persists the caller's travel mode and returns it.\n\n## Lifecycle, retries, and errors\n\n- All methods are idempotent except `addRoute` and `addTag`, which allocate a new id on every call. Retrying an `addRoute`/`addTag` after a timeout creates a duplicate record; retrying `updateRoute`, `updateTag`, `deleteRoute`, `deleteTag`, or `setTravelMode` is safe.\n- `deleteRoute` and `deleteTag` are destructive and irreversible.\n- Ownership is enforced on the backend: `updateRoute`, `updateTag`, `deleteRoute`, and `deleteTag` return `null`/`false` for ids the caller does not own rather than mutating another user's data.\n- Anonymous callers are rejected with a trap on every method.\n- `getApiDoc()` — query; returns this document.\n";
  };
};
